Preliminary Experiment Findings
1.	E6.5 is active in the current Step 6 flow and influences routing before completion review and final LLM call.
2.	Information-only detection is deterministic and prevents unnecessary downstream processing.
3.	Metadata-only template coverage is explicitly constrained to avoid overclaiming full coverage.
4.	Coverage outputs are exported and auditable through dedicated template coverage artifacts.
5.	Gap-based continuation improves focus by reducing template-covered noise in downstream reasoning.
Runtime and Production Gaps / Uncertainties
1.	Template identity dependency:
•	historical template mapping quality can vary by event and project linkage.
1.	Activity text quality:
•	template activities can be broad; line-item granularity mismatch remains a risk.
1.	LLM classification consistency:
•	overlap judgments may vary across edge cases without stronger normalization and guardrails.
1.	Metadata-only limitations:
•	limited line-item evidence forces conservative outcomes and higher unclear rates.
1.	Cross-stage governance:
•	need clear policy ownership for when to force manual review vs continue automatically.
Usage Guidance
Use E6.5 outputs as:
•	a pre-applicability dedup and routing stage
•	a way to isolate net-new TIL scope from standard-template scope
Do not use E6.5 outputs as:
•	final applicability or implementation-status verdicts
•	substitute for service-history evidence checks
